# International Labour Organization (ILO) Vulnerability Disclosure

# The ILO welcomes reports of security vulnerabilities and information
# security incidents affecting its digital assets. Responsible disclosure
# helps us protect the Organization, its constituents, and the public.

Contact: mailto:cybersecurity@ilo.org
Preferred-Languages: en, fr, es
Canonical: https://www.ilo.org/.well-known/security.txt

# The ILO does not operate a bug bounty program

# Out of scope vulnerabilities
# - Clickjacking found on non-authenticated forms or non-sensitive actions
# - Cross-Site Scripting or unencoded characters found on non-authenticated forms or non-sensitive actions - unless an additional security impact can be demonstrated
# - Any activity that could lead to the disruption of our service (DoS)
# - Cross-Site Request Forgery (CSRF) on unauthenticated forms or forms with no sensitive actions
# - Missing best practices in SSL/TLS configuration
